# TLS trust-store knobs.
#
# Stock ESP8266_RTOS_SDK v3.4 references CONFIG_MBEDTLS_CERTIFICATE_BUNDLE in
# esp_tls_mbedtls.c (it gates both the #include "esp_crt_bundle.h" and the
# cfg->crt_bundle_attach() call) but never declares the symbol anywhere. This
# component declares it so the sdkconfig.defaults assignment activates the
# attach hook used by both esp_crt_bundle_attach (CA bundle) and
# pinned_tls_attach (leaf-fingerprint pinning).
#
# CONFIG_MBEDTLS_V3 is declared here too: v3.4 only ships mbedTLS v2 sources, so
# the symbol is an informational selector kept so the documented sdkconfig
# baseline (architecture doc 3.2) configures without an "unknown symbol"
# warning. The actual crypto runs on the in-tree v2 mbedtls; the attach hook,
# fingerprint pinning and CA bundle all use APIs present in v2.

menu "E-ink Todo TLS trust"

    config MBEDTLS_CERTIFICATE_BUNDLE
        bool "Enable the mbedTLS certificate-bundle attach hook"
        default y
        help
            Activates esp_tls_mbedtls.c's crt_bundle_attach path. Required for
            both the curated CA bundle (esp_crt_bundle) and the pinned_tls leaf
            fingerprint verifier, which share the patched esp_http_client /
            tcp_transport crt_bundle_attach hook (R4/R5).

    config MBEDTLS_V3
        bool "Prefer mbedTLS v3 (informational; v3.4 ships v2 only)"
        default y
        help
            Tier-1 TLS selector from the architecture baseline. ESP8266_RTOS_SDK
            v3.4 only provides mbedTLS v2; this flag is kept so the committed
            sdkconfig.defaults configures cleanly. The trust paths use only
            APIs available in the in-tree v2 mbedtls. Disable together with
            CONFIG_MBEDTLS_CERTIFICATE_BUNDLE and enable CONFIG_EINKTODO_TLS_TIER2
            to fall back to the esp-tls global CA store (no SDK patch).

endmenu
